				776,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement WebviewView proxy for registerWebviewViewProvider API\n\nAdd the WebviewView proxy factory to support the VS Code extension API `vscode.window.registerWebviewViewProvider`. When an extension registers a webview view provider, Cocoon now creates a fresh `WebviewView` proxy object that bridges extension-side property writes and method calls to Mountain notifications.\n\nThe proxy implements:\n- `view.webview.html` setter → sends `webview.setHtml` to Mountain → Sky applies to workbench WebviewView\n- `view.webview.postMessage(msg)` → sends `webview.postMessage` to Mountain\n- `view.webview.onDidReceiveMessage` → wires up listener channel for messages from Sky\n- `view.show()` → sends `webview.reveal` notification to Mountain\n- `view.onDidChangeVisibility` / `view.onDispose` → lifecycle event support\n\nEach `resolveWebviewView` call gets a new proxy instance to prevent event subscription leakage across resolves. The `WebviewViewBuilders` map is indexed by handle alongside `WebviewViewProviders` for single-step lookup during `webview.resolveView` handling.\n\nExtensions can now use the WebviewView API with their UI rendered in the parked workbench.",
			"SHA": "d0f26f734bafed0d572cd0dff4ac28426edc824f"
		}
	],
